cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below."
title: "IBB: Information-Borrowing Bayesian covariance estimation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of IBB, a Bayesian framework for estimating a
  population covariance matrix when the number of variables far exceeds the
  number of samples. Marginal variances and correlation calibration are
  estimated jointly through an O(d) node-wise parameterization, with a
  Woodbury factorization reducing each HMC iteration to O(n^2 d).
